Subject: [PATCH] tests: initialize mastering peak sentinel for optimized GCC
 builds

The getter intentionally leaves its out value untouched for unknown peaks. Initialize the test local to an impossible physical value so optimized distribution builds with -Werror can prove it is defined. Keep both success/failure assertions and all measured expectations unchanged.
---
 src/tests/wayland-color-management-test.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/tests/wayland-color-management-test.c b/src/tests/wayland-color-management-test.c
index f8e8ae5..6665eba 100644
--- a/src/tests/wayland-color-management-test.c
+++ b/src/tests/wayland-color-management-test.c
@@ -1007,7 +1007,7 @@ mastering_round_trip (void)
   g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) plain = NULL;
   ClutterColorState *color_state;
   const ClutterColorTargetVolume *target_volume;
-  double peak;
+  double peak = -1.0;
 
   /* The client also checks the advertised features. */
   client = meta_wayland_test_client_new_with_args (test_context,
